A record whose `type:` differs from its directory gets a `frontmatter` finding on the `type:`
key's line. The value schema pins `type: value`, so mdcheck reports the same key as well.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/value/0001-first.md --
---
title: First
type: rule
summary: The first value.
kind: value
created_by: owner
created_at: 2026-01-01
updated_at: 2026-01-01
---

Why the project exists.

## In practice

It shows in every run.
-- cmd --
booping specs check
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
vault/value/0001-first.md:3  error  frontmatter  type is `rule`, the directory is `value`
vault/value/0001-first.md:3  error  schema  `type` value `rule` does not match `value`
-- stderr --
1 record(s) checked: 2 error(s), 0 warning(s)
